3. Problem Definition

Project owners often know that they need creative work but do not have a fast, clear path to the right outcome.

The current process is fragmented. Users may need to:

browse large numbers of creative profiles;

move between multiple platforms;

interpret specialist design terminology;

compare creatives without a consistent system;

coordinate different creatives separately; and

manage files, feedback, revisions, approvals, and delivery through disconnected tools.

The difficulty increases when one project requires several creative services. A restaurant or café, for example, may need visual identity, menu design, packaging, social-media assets, digital displays, motion graphics, staff products, and artwork. Finding and coordinating separate creatives can consume time and produce an inconsistent visual result.

Clients also have different levels of urgency and complexity:

Some need a fast, usable design they can customize immediately.

Others need an original solution developed by a professional.

Multi-service projects may require one multidisciplinary studio or a coordinated team.

Existing experiences often force these users through the same journey. TENTORA separates the two needs while keeping them connected.

4. TENTORA Concept

TENTORA is an AI-powered, curated creative-solutions platform that helps project owners move from a creative need to a usable result through a visual, simple, and organized experience.

The platform begins with the client's project sector and required service, not an open directory of creative profiles.

After selecting a service, the client chooses the path that fits the need:

Design Now: Customize a ready interactive design and obtain an immediate result.

Work With a Creative: Discover a visual direction and work with a compatible creative, studio, or coordinated team.

TENTORA connects four capabilities:

sector-based service discovery;

interactive ready-design customization;

visual taste understanding and intelligent creative matching; and

project organization from selection to delivery.

AI does not remove the role of artists and designers. It reduces friction, accelerates permitted customization, structures visual preferences, improves matching, supports project coordination, and enables a smooth transition from self-service design to professional execution.

Product boundary

TENTORA is not a conventional freelance marketplace, generic template library, random portfolio feed, or blank-canvas AI image generator. Its role is to curate, understand, connect, and organize creative outcomes.

5. Initial Target Sectors

The initial version focuses on five project sectors. The selected sector determines which services, ready designs, creative work, and recommendations are shown. This prevents the experience from becoming a large, generic catalogue.

