19. Stage 1 Decisions and Exit Criteria

19.1 Approved product decisions

TENTORA uses five initial sectors to organize discovery.

TENTORA offers two connected paths: Design Now and Work With a Creative.

Design Now begins with a Ready Interactive Design, not a blank canvas or full taste test.

Every custom project has one Main Taste Profile by default.

A service may have an optional refinement without repeating the full test.

Recommendation results are limited to six creative, studio, or team options.

Self-service work can move into professional execution without restarting.

Creators retain attribution, ownership, and defined commercial rights.

AI supports customization, understanding, matching, handoff, and coordination; it does not replace human authorship and craft.

19.2 Items to approve in Stage 2

exact Phase 1 MVP scope;

pilot services and Ready Design types;

named stakeholders and role capacity;

deliverables and acceptance criteria;

validated success metrics;

delivery schedule and budget boundaries;

governance, escalation, and decision rights; and

legal entity and ownership structure.

19.3 Exit criterion

Stage 1 is complete when the project sponsor and core team accept the product definition and authorize Stage 2 to convert it into a bounded project charter.

